# Arena Set Cracker (frontend)

## Product

Offline-first Angular app for managing **Magic: The Gathering Arena** decks within **one installed set at a time**.

Happy path: install a set (Scryfall) → open it → paste an Arena deck export → persist locally → reload and still see the list.

**Invariant:** decks and Arena imports resolve only against the focused set’s catalog. Lines that do not match that catalog are stripped; notify the user. Do not design for multi-set decklists.

## Stack map

- Angular 20 standalone + Material
- Local DB: Drizzle schema → sql.js (browser IndexedDB / Electron file)
- Platform wiring: `SQLITE_ENGINE_TOKEN`, `DATA_WIRE_TOKEN` (`CloudDataWire` vs `ElectronDataWire`)
- Also: Capacitor mobile, optional cloud API via `src/assets/config.json` (`baseUrl`)

## Where the brain lives

| Concern | Owner |
|---------|--------|
| Installed sets + active workspace (set, cards, decks) | `SetService` |
| Active deck scratchpad + flush/persist | `DeckService` |
| Arena parse + name resolve within catalog | `shared/models/deck/deck.utils.ts` |
| SQLite schema / migrations | `core/sqlite/sqlite.schema.ts`, `public/drizzle/` |
| Shared CSS shell (auth/forms) | `shared/styles/auth-shell.css`, tokens in `styles.css` |

## Commits

Ask where the user is before committing. First line: `<place> <goal>` (Hideaway is a place-stamp, not a magic title and not assumed).

Body only when the goal needs grains above the diff—how it was achieved across components. A self-explanatory diff (one file, obvious) is header-only; do not restate the header.

Fold same-story follow-ups into the unpushed commit. Leave unrelated fixes as their own commit. Do not rewrite anything already on the remote.

Only commit when the user asks.

## Session scope

Treat cloud sync polish, art download/Capacitor filesystem, and similar as **in or out of scope only when the user says so** for that session—do not assume they are permanent non-goals.
